command_board_tui.py — native Linux, pure stdlib. Same curses library htop uses. Just python3 command_board_tui.py and it runs. No pip, no apt, no network. Python 3 ships on every Linux I know of, including rescue rootfs. Tested in the sandbox: Ctrl+C exits with code 0, files save atomically, no stderr noise.

